    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d743">

                <pb facs="0856" n="1690" xml:id="pg1690"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/1196a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-22T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 22, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>342. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 901. Your 1032, Embassy’s 378, July 17, 5 p.m. We think it best to accept the
                    British suggestions respecting the functions of the Inter-Allied Purchasing
                    Bureau in Spain, hoping that as time goes on they will find it possible to agree
                    to an extension of the bureau’s powers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
